We have a skeleton HTML page with no script. Task 2 requires adding code for game state objects and constants, with plain object literals for player, hazards array, score, phase, and constants at top of script, setting initial values.

The reference template defines a bunch of sections: CONFIG, STATE, RESET, UPDATE, RENDER, INPUT, AUDIO, OBSERVABLE CONTRACT, BOOT. We need to adjust the placeholder script accordingly, adding these sections. We have to preserve the structure "section divider banners" with // === SECTION === lines.

We need to edit index.html (script part) to include the new code; but must not rewrite entire file from scratch. So we need to edit the content inside <script> tags. Add sections accordingly.

Specifically, we need at the top of script (i.e., after script tag begins) define constants (CONFIG), then state variables (e.g., canvas, ctx, restartBtn), then a reset function initializing state objects: player, hazards array, score, phase, keys set, lastTime, etc.

But the task specifically says: "Game state objects — define plain object literals for player, hazards array, score, phase, and constants at top of script, setting initial values."

Thus we need to add const definitions for game behavior.

Constraints: No console errors. Particular note: In reference they have canvas and context selection; they have a restart button element. Those need to be defined for later tasks but we might not need to define them yet, but to avoid errors when page loads we should keep them functional: we can define them as variables and assign them in script. But our placeholder script currently contains only comment: // Game script will be added in later tasks.

If we just add constants and state objects, we must also maybe query the DOM to get canvas, ctx, etc, else later code (when more tasks added) may refer to them. But currently only initial loading must not cause errors. If we query elements right away, that will be fine.

Thus we should add code like:

// === CONFIG =============================================================

const GRAVITY = 800; // px/sec^2?

But we need to decide what constants to set. We should follow reference style: define constants for player dimensions, pipe sizes etc. However the task only says "constants at top of script, setting initial values." Possibly we need to define constants like PLAYER_R = 6; PIPE_SPEED = 200; etc. But we need to obey the reference template structure: the divider banners must follow the fixed order: CONFIG → STATE → RESET → LOOP/UPDATE → RENDER → INPUT → AUDIO → OBSERVABLE CONTRACT → BOOT.

Since we haven't reached later tasks, we can include only the sections needed: Config, State, Reset, maybe Boot? But the code must still not cause errors. We can define stub functions for others (e.g., startLoop). But no need, they will be added later. However we need to ensure no references to undefined variables.

Thus minimal approach: Insert code with Config, State, Reset, Boot (call reset). And compute a placeholder reset that sets initial values.

