Define reset function that initializes player (x set initial horizontal position, maybe 100; y at half of canvas height). We'll need to get canvas dimensions after DOM is ready. Since script is at bottom of body after canvas and button, we can query them immediately.

Implementation: const canvas = document.getElementById('game'); const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d'); const restartBtn = document.getElementById('restart');

function reset() { player = { x: 100, y: canvas.height / 2, vy: 0 }; hazards = []; score = 0; phase = "playing"; keys = new Set(); lastTime = performance.now(); // maybe set up event listeners: restartBtn.addEventListener('click', reset); // also key listeners.

Could be later tasks adding more, but we can set them now to avoid later duplication. The guidelines say we must preserve everything, but modifications are allowed.

